{
  "case_id": "2008-07-772",
  "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (William B. Collins)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit decision should be reversed because the Washington court's adjudication of this matter was not objectively unreasonable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, is there some constitutional minimum? Let's assume direct review. Is there some constitutional minimum requirement for scienter with reference to an accomplice?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (William B. Collins)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the prosecutor argued that Mr. Sarausad acted with knowledge that he was facilitating a homicide."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes, but isn't the problem on your side of the case that there was another \"in for a dime, in for a dollar\" argument and that was the hypothetical holding the hands behind the back while some third party slugged the victim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the same -- and hadn't the prosecutors in Washington in misstating the standard the same way and using \"In for a dime, in for a dollar\" to mean precisely the wrong thing, namely that even if you were in for beating him up that's enough for holding you liable for homicide?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0000-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The point. It asked for further instructions three times on this precise point, what did -- did he have to know. And all the trial judge did was say read, you know, read my instructions, which essentially recited the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0000-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Excuse me. Let's go back to 131 for a minute. I thought that applied to the \"accomplice\" instruction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0000-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Did both -- do you have to have the same intent as -- does the accomplice have to have the same intent as the principal?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But we already know that many people, prosecutors, justices, misunderstood this \"a crime.\" Was it \"a crime,\" or \"any crime.\" Or \"the crime\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Collins",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. COLLINS: Your Honor, we are not arguing that there couldn't be some ambiguity, but what we are saying is that the adjudication by the PRP court was not objectively unreasonable. Because when you look at the instructions as a whole and the argument as a whole and the evidence as a whole, the PRP court's decision is not objectively unreasonable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: The gloss that the Washington Supreme Court ended up with was exactly the same as the instruction that was, that the judge gave in this case -- to be as a -- the trial judge, whatever the state of the law was, got it right."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: So it is not objectively unreasonable for the State to instruct jurors as they did? If that's all you had, then that would be the point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The prosecutor, I mean I thought, though I'm not -- this really is ambiguous, I think, but if you do hold somebody's arms behind his back and punch him in the stomach, that does perhaps -- at least might run -- I can see a person saying that that runs a substantial risk of death. I mean Houdini died that way, apparently. So maybe hitting somebody in the stomach does create a substantial risk of death. Do you know anything about -- one way or the other on that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Second degree murder is intentional."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "With the jury -- was the jury told that the arguments of counsel are not the law, that I, the judge, will tell you what the law is?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So what's the relevance of it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-663e6d6ceb1b-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it your view that the question that is troubling the jury was whether they had to find that the driver of the car knew that there was a gun in the car."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-772",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "663e6d6ceb1bb2188e2aa36a2578d9dc684a8f4e390be8c0e0d3d14d640129e9",
